Home feature carousel: use box-shadow instead of filter: drop-shadow().

Under GPU rasterization the drop-shadow filter's enlarged raster bounds are
not reliably invalidated when the carousel swaps pages, leaving torn fragments
of previously shown album art painted around each cover. box-shadow renders
identically on this opaque, clipped, rounded container and has no such issue.

Upstream: https://github.com/jeffvli/feishin (branch fix/carousel-drop-shadow-artifacts)

diff --git a/src/renderer/components/feature-carousel/feature-carousel.module.css b/src/renderer/components/feature-carousel/feature-carousel.module.css
index 21ee9994..52296ef2 100644
--- a/src/renderer/components/feature-carousel/feature-carousel.module.css
+++ b/src/renderer/components/feature-carousel/feature-carousel.module.css
@@ -181,8 +181,19 @@
     max-width: 120px;
     overflow: hidden;
     border-radius: var(--theme-radius-md);
-    filter: drop-shadow(0 6px 20px rgb(0 0 0 / 50%)) drop-shadow(0 2px 8px rgb(0 0 0 / 40%));
-    transition: filter 0.3s ease;
+
+    /*
+     * Use box-shadow, not filter: drop-shadow(). The container is an opaque,
+     * fully-clipped rounded rectangle, so the two render identically -- but
+     * drop-shadow costs an offscreen filter pass and enlarges the layer's raster
+     * bounds. With GPU rasterization those enlarged bounds are not reliably
+     * invalidated when the carousel swaps pages, leaving torn fragments of the
+     * previous album art painted around each cover.
+     */
+    box-shadow:
+        0 6px 20px rgb(0 0 0 / 50%),
+        0 2px 8px rgb(0 0 0 / 40%);
+    transition: box-shadow 0.3s ease;
 }
 
 .single-carousel-container .album-image-container {
@@ -217,13 +228,17 @@
 
 .carousel-item:hover .album-image-container,
 .carousel-link:hover .album-image-container {
-    filter: drop-shadow(0 16px 40px rgb(0 0 0 / 60%)) drop-shadow(0 6px 16px rgb(0 0 0 / 50%));
+    box-shadow:
+        0 16px 40px rgb(0 0 0 / 60%),
+        0 6px 16px rgb(0 0 0 / 50%);
 }
 
 /* Single carousel: remove hover shadow effect */
 .single-carousel-container .carousel-item:hover .album-image-container,
 .single-carousel-container .carousel-link:hover .album-image-container {
-    filter: drop-shadow(0 6px 20px rgb(0 0 0 / 50%)) drop-shadow(0 2px 8px rgb(0 0 0 / 40%));
+    box-shadow:
+        0 6px 20px rgb(0 0 0 / 50%),
+        0 2px 8px rgb(0 0 0 / 40%);
 }
 
